<title>SWITZERLAND: ALPINE SKIING-SYKORA WINS MEN'S WORLD CUP SLALOM.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-SYKORA WINS MEN'S WORLD CUP SLALOM.</headline>
<dateline>WENGEN, Switzerland 1997-01-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austria's Thomas Sykora won his fifth men's Alpine World Cup slalom of the season on Sunday when he clocked a two-run combined time of one minute 34.03 seconds.</p>
<p>Thomas Stangassinger of Austria was second in 1:34.36 and Sebastien Amiez of France finished third in 1:34.68, according to unofficial results.</p>
